Subject: Keep the greeter across a VT switch, and start again a greeter that exits with no login

The greeter quits once its last window is gone, and its compositor can
drop every output across a VT switch: leaving the greeter's VT for a text
console and coming back ends the greeter. The daemon starts a greeter
again only after a display-server, tty or session error, so the display
stays black with no password field until sddm itself is restarted.

Outside test mode the greeter quits only when the daemon stops it, when
its socket closes, or when a login succeeds; a closed last window or a
released event-loop lock ends nothing.

The daemon starts a greeter again that exits while nobody logs in on its
display and nobody asked it to stop, once the display's VT is in front
again: sddm-helper activates the greeter's VT as it starts it, and would
pull a user off the console they switched to. Three exits in a row, each
within a minute of its start, end the retries.

